{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeBoundedFullTwist","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeBoundedFullTwist","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeBoundedJucysMurphy","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeFullTwistProduct"],"declarations":23,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.stdTwoBelow3_jmProd_eq_fullTwist","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.stdTwoBelow3_jmProd_eq_fullTwist","kind":"theorem","line":288,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedFullTwist.lean#L288-L297","doc":"**What the port bought.**  `L₀L₁L₂ = (σ₀σ₁)³` — the full twist of `B₃` — holds on the\n2-dimensional `(2,1)` representation of `H₃(q)`.\n\n`HeckeStableScalarCascade.stdTwo_no_stable_extension` proves the *unbounded* presentation cannot\nhost this representation at all, so this instance of `∏Lᵢ = Δ²` is unreachable from\n`jmProd_eq_delta_pow`.  It is exactly the content the bounded port adds. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.stdTwoBelow3_deltaB_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.stdTwoBelow3_deltaB_two","kind":"theorem","line":283,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedFullTwist.lean#L283-L286","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmProd_eq_delta_pow_of_below","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmProd_eq_delta_pow_of_below","kind":"theorem","line":271,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedFullTwist.lean#L271-L275","doc":"Recovers `jmProd_eq_delta_pow` from the bounded form: take `n` past `k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmProdB_toBelow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmProdB_toBelow","kind":"theorem","line":266,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedFullTwist.lean#L266-L269","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmProdB_eq_deltaB_pow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmProdB_eq_deltaB_pow","kind":"theorem","line":247,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedFullTwist.lean#L247-L262","doc":"**`∏Lᵢ = Δ²` on the bounded presentation.**  `L₀⋯L_k = (deltaB k)^{k+1}`, the full twist of\n`B_{k+1}`, for every `k < n`.\n\nAt `n = 3` this is `L₀L₁L₂ = (σ₀σ₁)³` — the `H₃(q)` case, now available on a presentation the\n2-dimensional representation actually satisfies. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmProdB_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmProdB_succ","kind":"theorem","line":244,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedFullTwist.lean#L244-L245","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmProdB","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmProdB","kind":"def","line":239,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedFullTwist.lean#L239-L242","doc":"The ordered product `L₀L₁⋯L_{k−1}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRawB_eq_run_mul_delta","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRawB_eq_run_mul_delta","kind":"theorem","line":229,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedFullTwist.lean#L229-L237","doc":"`Lₖ = runB 0 k · deltaB k`.  **No relation is used** — the recursion alone, so no bound. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.deltaB_twist_step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.deltaB_twist_step","kind":"theorem","line":220,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedFullTwist.lean#L220-L225","doc":"**The twist step**, bounded. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.deltaB_pow_run","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.deltaB_pow_run","kind":"theorem","line":197,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedFullTwist.lean#L197-L218","doc":"**The power identity**, bounded: `(deltaB m · σ_m)^{k+1} = (deltaB m)^{k+1} · runB b (k+1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.runB_push","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.runB_push","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedFullTwist.lean#L147-L195","doc":"**The push law**, bounded.  The induction reaches index `p + 1 = m`, and the braid relation\nthere needs `m + 2 < n`; hence the hypothesis `m + 1 < n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.core_braid_pushB","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.core_braid_pushB","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedFullTwist.lean#L127-L143","doc":"The push law's core braid step.  Uses `far b (m+1)` and `braid m`, both needing `m + 2 < n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.sigma_comm_deltaB","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.sigma_comm_deltaB","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedFullTwist.lean#L109-L125","doc":"`σⱼ` commutes with `deltaB m` when `m < j`.  Needs `σⱼ` to be a generator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.sigma_comm_runB","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.sigma_comm_runB","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedFullTwist.lean#L90-L107","doc":"`σⱼ` commutes with a descending run sitting `≥ 2` below it.  Needs `σⱼ` to be a generator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.runB_peel_bot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.runB_peel_bot","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedFullTwist.lean#L76-L86","doc":"Peeling the run from the bottom.  **No relation is used** — this is the recursion alone, so no\nindex bound is required. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.runB_toBelow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.runB_toBelow","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedFullTwist.lean#L71-L74","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.deltaB_toBelow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.deltaB_toBelow","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedFullTwist.lean#L66-L69","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.runB_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.runB_succ","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedFullTwist.lean#L63-L64","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.runB_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.runB_zero","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedFullTwist.lean#L61-L61","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.deltaB_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.deltaB_succ","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedFullTwist.lean#L58-L59","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.deltaB_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.deltaB_zero","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedFullTwist.lean#L56-L56","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.runB","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.runB","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedFullTwist.lean#L51-L54","doc":"**Descending run** `runB b k = σ_{b+k−1} ⋯ σ_b`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.deltaB","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.deltaB","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedFullTwist.lean#L46-L49","doc":"**Ascending run** `deltaB k = σ₀ σ₁ ⋯ σ_{k−1}`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}